== 2.6 Chapter 2 Practice Drill — 40 Questions

40 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 44 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [Money is best defined as anything that is],
  [made of paper or metal],
  [issued by a government],
  [generally acceptable as a means of payment],
  [backed by gold reserves]
)

#mcq(2, [The function of money that eliminates the double coincidence of wants is],
  [store of value],
  [medium of exchange],
  [unit of account],
  [standard of deferred payment]
)

#mcq(3, [When prices are quoted in a single monetary unit, money is serving as a],
  [unit of account],
  [means of deferred payment],
  [medium of exchange],
  [store of value]
)

#mcq(4, [Money's usefulness as a store of value is most seriously weakened by],
  [an increase in the money supply alone],
  [a rise in the interest rate],
  [the use of cheques],
  [rapid inflation]
)

#mcq(5, [The function that makes lending and borrowing possible is money as a],
  [standard of deferred payment],
  [unit of account],
  [measure of value],
  [medium of exchange]
)

#mcq(6, [The quality of money that conflicts most with its function as a store of value is its],
  [divisibility],
  [liquidity],
  [portability],
  [durability]
)

#mcq(7, [Which of the following is the most liquid asset?],
  [a house],
  [a fixed deposit],
  [cash],
  [government bonds]
)

#mcq(8, [Legal tender means money that],
  [is issued by commercial banks],
  [is backed by gold],
  [must be accepted in settlement of a debt],
  [earns interest]
)

#mcq(9, [Commercial banks create credit when they],
  [buy treasury bills],
  [print additional currency],
  [borrow from the central bank],
  [lend out part of the deposits they hold]
)

#mcq(10, [If the cash reserve ratio is 20 per cent, the credit multiplier is],
  [0.2],
  [5],
  [20],
  [2]
)

#mcq(11, [A bank receives a deposit of ₦20,000 and the reserve ratio is 25 per cent. Total deposits created are],
  [₦100,000],
  [₦20,000],
  [₦80,000],
  [₦5,000]
)

#mcq(12, [An increase in the cash reserve ratio will],
  [reduce bank lending],
  [increase bank lending],
  [increase the money supply],
  [leave bank lending unchanged]
)

#mcq(13, [The credit multiplier is smaller than theory suggests when],
  [all borrowers deposit their loans in the same bank],
  [the reserve ratio is low],
  [banks hold excess reserves and the public holds cash],
  [the central bank buys securities]
)

#mcq(14, [The central bank of a country is described as the lender of last resort because it],
  [lends to the public at the lowest rate],
  [lends only for long-term projects],
  [lends to the government only],
  [lends to banks that cannot raise funds elsewhere]
)

#mcq(15, [Which of the following is NOT a function of the central bank?],
  [issuing currency],
  [accepting deposits from the general public],
  [acting as banker to the government],
  [managing the external reserves]
)

#mcq(16, [The bank that holds the accounts of the federal government and manages its debt is the],
  [commercial bank],
  [development bank],
  [merchant bank],
  [central bank]
)

#mcq(17, [Open market operations involve the central bank],
  [setting the cash reserve ratio],
  [buying and selling government securities],
  [fixing the exchange rate],
  [persuading banks to lend]
)

#mcq(18, [To reduce inflation the central bank would],
  [lend more to commercial banks],
  [sell securities and raise the reserve ratio],
  [buy securities and lower the reserve ratio],
  [lower the policy rate]
)

#mcq(19, [The instrument sometimes described as moral suasion is],
  [persuasion of banks to follow the central bank's wishes],
  [changes in the reserve ratio],
  [open market operations],
  [changes in the exchange rate]
)

#mcq(20, [Inflation is best defined as],
  [a rise in the price of one commodity],
  [a sustained rise in the general price level],
  [an increase in the money supply],
  [a fall in the value of the currency abroad]
)

#mcq(21, [Inflation caused by an increase in aggregate demand beyond the economy's capacity is called],
  [cost-push inflation],
  [demand-pull inflation],
  [structural inflation],
  [imported inflation]
)

#mcq(22, [A sharp rise in the price of imported raw materials is most likely to cause],
  [a fall in the price level],
  [deflation],
  [demand-pull inflation],
  [cost-push inflation]
)

#mcq(23, [Cost-push inflation is more difficult to cure than demand-pull because],
  [it cannot be measured],
  [the usual anti-inflationary policies also reduce output and employment],
  [it only affects the rich],
  [it does not affect the price level]
)

#mcq(24, [During a period of rapid inflation, the group that gains is],
  [debtors on fixed-interest loans],
  [holders of fixed-interest bonds],
  [savers with money in current accounts],
  [pensioners on fixed incomes]
)

#mcq(25, [Which group suffers most from inflation?],
  [borrowers with variable-rate loans],
  [holders of real assets],
  [traders who can reprice daily],
  [people on fixed money incomes]
)

#mcq(26, [Deflation is],
  [a sustained fall in the general price level],
  [a fall in the value of money],
  [a fall in the rate of inflation],
  [a rise in the exchange rate]
)

#mcq(27, [One danger of deflation is that consumers],
  [postpone spending in the hope of lower prices still],
  [lose their savings to banks],
  [cannot borrow at all],
  [spend more in anticipation of lower prices]
)

#mcq(28, [The quantity theory of money states that, other things being equal, a rise in the money supply leads to],
  [a proportional rise in the price level],
  [a fall in output],
  [a fall in the price level],
  [no change in prices]
)

#mcq(29, [Which measure is used to track inflation in Nigeria?],
  [the exchange rate],
  [the human development index],
  [the consumer price index],
  [the balance of payments]
)

#mcq(30, [A rise in the policy rate is intended to],
  [encourage borrowing and spending],
  [discourage borrowing and reduce aggregate demand],
  [increase government spending],
  [lower the exchange rate]
)

#mcq(31, [Near money is best described as],
  [notes and coins in circulation],
  [currency that is no longer legal tender],
  [assets that can be converted into cash quickly with little loss],
  [money held in foreign accounts]
)

#mcq(32, [The money supply is likely to rise when],
  [commercial banks lend more],
  [the reserve ratio is increased],
  [the public holds more cash outside the banks],
  [the central bank sells securities]
)

#mcq(33, [A commercial bank's main source of profit is the],
  [difference between the interest it pays depositors and charges borrowers],
  [revenue from treasury bill purchases],
  [profit from printing currency],
  [fee for holding government accounts]
)

#mcq(34, [Bank runs are dangerous because banks],
  [hold long-term loans against short-term deposits],
  [lend only to the government],
  [cannot create credit],
  [hold all deposits in cash]
)

#mcq(35, [Which is an example of an asset that is highly liquid but a poor store of value over a long period?],
  [a plot of land],
  [a factory building],
  [a ten-year bond],
  [cash in a current account]
)

#mcq(36, [If the reserve ratio falls from 25 per cent to 20 per cent, the credit multiplier],
  [stays at 5],
  [rises from 4 to 5],
  [falls from 5 to 4],
  [falls to 0.2]
)

#mcq(37, [An economy has excess demand and rising prices. The appropriate combination of policies is],
  [cut taxes, raise spending, buy securities],
  [cut taxes and sell securities],
  [raise taxes, reduce spending, sell securities],
  [raise spending and lower the reserve ratio]
)

#mcq(38, [A rise in the general price level that is caused by a devaluation is best described as],
  [deflation],
  [disinflation],
  [demand-pull inflation],
  [imported inflation]
)

#mcq(39, [Which statement about inflation and unemployment is correct?],
  [there is no relationship of any kind],
  [a short-run trade-off exists but the curve can shift],
  [the Phillips curve shows a permanent trade-off],
  [the two always move together]
)

#mcq(40, [Which of the following is a liability of a commercial bank?],
  [a customer's savings deposit],
  [a loan to a manufacturer],
  [a holding of treasury bills],
  [cash in the vault]
)

